## New Capabilities Identified

- **Done toggle button** — the per-row check-in control becomes a button reading
  "Done today" (neutral outlined) when today is not completed and "Done ✓" (success
  green) when it is. Behavior is unchanged: same toggle semantics, same idempotent
  store mutation, same streak recomputation. This rewrites the TOR-03 checkbox
  Given/When/Then wording.
- **Streak caption** — the streak badge gains a "DAY STREAK" caption beneath the
  number on every row (active and archived). Refines TOR-04-5xu6Aag /
  TOR-07-pa7ak24 presentation.
- **Streak-rule help hint** — new static copy above the list on the Active view:
  "Mark done tomorrow to continue a streak — a missed day resets it to 1." No
  existing TOR covers it; needs a new TOR ID.

## Priority Signal

Visual/UX parity with the sibling Summit implementation is the goal; **behavior,
data model, and dependencies are unchanged**. The one-hot-element rule (flame accent
reserved for the Add button) is explicitly preserved — the sibling's flame-accented
unchecked "Done today" treatment was considered and **rejected**; the unchecked
button is neutral outlined, the checked state is success green.

## Deferred Items

- Nothing else deferred this cycle; the flame-accent amendment option was rejected
  rather than deferred.
- Interview defaults were applied (no user feedback received during the session):
  Active-view-only help hint, caption on all rows, "Done today"/"Done ✓" labels.
  Adjustable at review before the docs branch merges.
